# GitLab Pages redirects from mike's published URLs (#1271 spike). Not deployed.
#
# mike published 22 version directories on gh-pages (see its versions.json)
# plus four aliases. mkdocs-material's version dropdown links to the
# full-version directories (/v1.2.0/, /v1.1.0/, ...), so those are the URLs
# people bookmarked, not just the aliases.
#
# Covered without a rule (same path on both sites):
#   /v1.2/, /v1.1/          mike's minor aliases = the starlight-versions slugs
#   /v1.2.0-alpha.1/        kept as an archived version in this prototype
#
# Splat rules keep the rest of the path, so a deep link lands on the same page
# in the matching version.
#   301  the target is the permanent home of that release's docs
#   302  the target is a stand-in that is expected to change: the two
#        floating aliases, and v1.0, which this prototype does not backfill
#
# Aliases. Today `latest` is mike's default and means the newest GA release,
# not main; keep that meaning by pointing it at the newest GA version (move it
# when a new minor is cut). `next` is mike's newest pre-release; this prototype
# serves main at the root, so `next` goes there. What the root itself should
# serve (newest GA, or main) is an open decision; see SPIKE-FINDINGS.md and #2019.
/latest/*            /v1.2/:splat    302
/next/*              /:splat         302

# 1.2 line -> /v1.2/
/v1.2.0/*            /v1.2/:splat    301
/v1.2.0-rc.1/*       /v1.2/:splat    301
/v1.2.0-beta.3/*     /v1.2/:splat    301
/v1.2.0-beta.2/*     /v1.2/:splat    301
/v1.2.0-beta.1/*     /v1.2/:splat    301
/v1.2.0-alpha.4/*    /v1.2/:splat    301
/v1.2.0-alpha.3/*    /v1.2/:splat    301
/v1.2.0-alpha.2/*    /v1.2/:splat    301

# 1.1 line -> /v1.1/
/v1.1.0/*            /v1.1/:splat    301
/v1.1.0-rc.3/*       /v1.1/:splat    301
/v1.1.0-rc.2/*       /v1.1/:splat    301
/v1.1.0-rc.1/*       /v1.1/:splat    301

# 1.0 line: no v1.0 snapshot in this prototype, so send it to the current
# docs for now. Backfill v1.0 (npm run snapshot -- v1.0.0 v1.0) and point
# these at /v1.0/:splat with 301 if 1.0 docs should stay reachable (#2019).
/v1.0.0/*            /:splat         302
/v1.0.0-rc.11/*      /:splat         302
/v1.0.0-rc.10/*      /:splat         302
/v1.0.0-rc.9/*       /:splat         302
/v1.0.0-rc.8/*       /:splat         302
/v1.0.0-rc.6/*       /:splat         302
/v1.0.0-rc.5/*       /:splat         302
/v1.0.0-rc.4/*       /:splat         302
/v1.0.0-rc.3/*       /:splat         302
